this is the unifed encrypted IAT Trampoline, every singel API Call regardless of dll goes through the same obfscuated dispatcher



5- Encrypted IAT ( Deeply a little lol )

5.1 Mechanism

Eidolon IAT Flow:

1- game code call [IAT_slot] all 31 dll IAT slots point to the same unifed trampoline at RVA 0x4AC878
2- Static dump shows placeholder bytes (0x000002B968630000), runtime shows resolved pointer (0x5CE9F34A36F45570)
3- On first call: Eidolon hashes the API name & DLL name, looks up the index, decrypts the real entry from .eid section, calls LdrGetProcedureAddress to resolve, caches the result
4- Subsequent calls: jumps directly to cached real API through the trampoline
5- Every single Win32 API call goes through this, zero direct imports exist


5.2 Runtime Verification

Static Dump API Content

RVA: 0x4AC878
Bytes: 00 00 00 63 B9 68 02 00 00 00
Interpretation: Obfuscated placeholder (not a valid pointer)

Runtime IAT Content

RVA: 0x005CC878
Bytes: 5C E9 F3 4A 36 F4 55 70
Interpretation: Resolved pointer to a real function or dispatcher stub

the runtime value 0x7055F4364AF3E95C (reversed for big-endian) is:
1- A valid usermode address (in the 0x7FFE... range after ASLR adjustment)
2- Actually points to a resolver stub in `.text that handles the API dispatch

5.3 Res Process

the IAT Res Happens in phases:

Phase 1, Static Load ( PE Loader )
Windows PE Loader sees the Decoy Import Table
Writes the Placeholder Trampoline addr to all IAT Slots
game starts with non functional IAT

Phase 2: Eidolon_Run Init
Decrypt the Real Import Mapping from .eid Section
For Each Required API: computes HASH -> looks up in .eid table -> gets api name -> resolves via LdrGetProcedureAddress
Patches the IAT Trampoline toredirect the resolved API
but does not overwrite the IAT Slots directly, uses a separate dispatch table

Phase 3: Lazy Res
some APIs are resolved lazily ( on first call )
the unfied trampoline checks a cache, resolves if needed then calls
cache entries are stored in the .data section

