6, Warden VEH Mechanism

6.1 Arch

Warden Uses VEH as its primary runtime enforcemnt mech, unlike SEH, VEH Operates at the Process level and receives exceptions before any frame based handlers


Exception Flow:
CPU Exception ( int3, access violation ) -> KiUserExceptionDispatcher (ntdll) -> VEH Chain ( first chance ) -> Warden VEH Handler ( Registered by TLS CB ) ->
INT3 from CFG Guard -> Validate + Emu
INT3 from Warden Patch -> Validate + Emu
INT3 from unknown -> Check Call site
other exception -> pass through

for the VEH Chain, -> Other VEH Handlers too.

for the KiUserExceptionDIspatcher, -> SEH Chain ( if VEH Returns CONTINUE_SEARCH )
KiUserExceptionDIspatcher -> UnHandledExceptionFilter, as a last resort.

6.2 VEH Registertion

func: RtlAddVectoredExceptionHandler in ntdll.dll
runtime addr: ntdll!0x0009DE30
caller: tls Callback 2 in overwatch.exe at 0x02665BB0
Handler Type: First chance VEH ( get exceptions before any debugger )


6.3 VEH Chain Structures ( win10 x64 )

struct _VECTORED_HANDLER_ENTRY {
LIST_ENTRY ListEntry; // +0x00: Flink (8) and Blink (8)
LONG RefCount; // +0x10: Reference count (4)
PVOID Handler; // +0x18: Function pointer (8)
ULONG_PTR Pad; // +0x20: Padding/alignment
};

struct _LIST_ENTRY {
LIST_ENTRY *Flink; // +0x00: Forward link
LIST_ENTRY *Blink; // +0x08: Backward link
};

The VEH chain head (RtlpVectoredHandlerList) is stored in ntdll's .data section. Walking this chain at runtime reveals all registered VEH handlers:

VEH 1: Handler=ntdll!RtlpExceptionHandler (default ntdll handler)
VEH 2: Handler=Overwatch.exe!WardenVEHHandler (Warden's handler)
VEH 3: Handler=... (any other registered handlers)

Note: On Windows 10 22H2+, the VEH chain may not be directly walkable from usermode without proper sync the chain is protected by a lock (RtlpVectoredHandlerLock).


6.4 INT3 Patch Mechanism

warden veh handler is designed to intercept int3 ( 0xcc ) exception, the mechanism:

1- warden patches game code, replaces legitmate intr bytes with 0xcc ( int3 )
2- when pathced code executes, int3 fires, KiUserExceptionDispatcher -> VEH Chain
3- warden handler Inspects exception:
address of int3 ( from EXCEPTIOn_RECORD.ExceptionAddress )
contents of surrounding memory
thread context ( registres )

4- if valid warden patch handler emulates the original instr
reads the saved original bytes from warden patch database
modfies thread context (context structures ) to emulate the instr
returns exception_continue_execution

5- if unknown int3 handler may:
return exception_contnue_search ( pass to other handlers )
log the violation for server side reporting
trigger integrity check failure ( MemoryTasHasFailed )


basic int3 distr analysis

static dump of overwatch.exe .text is like 1.2M Int3 bytes
runtime scan of overwatch.exe .text 0 int3 bytes
runtime scan of overwatch_loader.dll .text 24k int3 bytes

the 1.2M INT3 in static dump is CFG ( control flow guard ) not warden patches..




