7.2 Hash Table Mechanism

This is the most misunderstood aspect of Warden. The module names are stored in .rdata but are never referenced via direct LEA instructions. Instead, Warden uses a runtime hash table:

Hash Table Lookup:
Input: Module Name String -> Hash = HashFunction(ModuleName), Hash = CRC32 Variant or custom rolling
-> Index = Hash & (TableSize -1) -> Table[Index]:
Hash Stored
Module Entry Point
Module Metadata

if collision linear probing
result: module code addr or null

that explains why:
IDA Shows 0 xrefs to the module name strings
x64dbg cannot find refs via find ref to current
string search withen code does not help
the only way to find module loader is to:
1- find the hash func ( crc32 like custom poly )
2- breakpoint in memory access to the .rdata string area
3- trace back from the has comparision code


