7.4 Module Loader Hints

The Warden module loader was not fully resolved due to the encrypted IAT hiding VirtualAlloc calls. However, the following was determine

No NtAllocateVirtualMemory syscall found in the loaders .text sample, the loader either:
1. Uses an obfuscated wrapper around VirtualAlloc called through encrypted IAT
2. Uses memory within the existing module address space (no allocation needed)
3. Loads modules into pre allocated memory regions from initialization
The most likely approach is 3, Warden pre allocates a pool of RWX memory during initialization and loads scanning modules into this pool. This avoids runtime VirtualAlloc calls that could be hooked.


