8.3 Key Derivatin Chain

the decryption key is derived through a 4 layer transformation:

global_key = read_uint32(key_addr) // etc 0xC9EF16A9

layer1 = global_key ^ 0x4A772405
layer2 = (layer1 + 0x37022887) & 0xFFFFFFFF
layer3 = layer2 ^ 0x127F17B3
layer4 = (layer3 - global_key) & 0xFFFFFFFF

Each layer is used for a different phase of the decryption:
Layer 1: Initial string XOR mask
Layer 2: Address/offset obfuscation
Layer 3: Final XOR pass
Layer 4: Checksum validation

